phase('Build')
const mkBuild = (extra) => done('build:keepred') || agent(RULES + '\nRole: Doer (rules.md section (a)) for ' + d.row + ': ' + SPEC_D + '.' + IFACE_NOTE + ' Branch ' + BB + ', suffix vg-keepred, from origin/main; merge origin/' + tests.branch + rulingMerge() + extra + '.\nEdit ONLY: ' + d.product.join(', ') + ' (the owner row ' + d.row + ' also owns ' + testFiles.join(', ') + ': that is the test writer\'s, you never edit it). Build exactly what the scope says: a red playthrough or lane_plays stage keeps the pytest -rA output and every qa/*.png under SCRATCH_ROOT in the run directory of the ruling (T1 to T3; outside SCRATCH_ROOT, never /tmp); the CLI prints the EVIDENCE line and merge_gate.sh prints `GATE evidence kept: <path>` right after the REJECT line (T4); only a rejecting stage keeps evidence (T5); a green stage leaves nothing (T6); `merge_gate.sh --prune-evidence` and the weekly cleanup line in ' + DRIFT_AUDIT + ' (T7); the MALLOC_PERTURB_=255 prefix on the csim and transport regression commands, the suite_key fold in merge_gate_support.py and the env line of REPORT.txt (T8); the size cap (T9); evidence only from the CLI path, the bare functions unchanged; no unguarded $HOME in new bash (the default root and the prune live in Python); merge_gate.sh\'s trap leaves the directory alone (change the trap only if a stage needs it, and then only to NOT remove it). FACTS: ' + d.facts + ' Size: ' + d.cost + '. Numbers: only the row\'s, the ruling\'s and existing constants with file:line (name each in the code); a number or path the ruling does not give stops you with stop_reason "spec-gap: <what>". Comments only where non-obvious; where B exists because A fails, say so at both sites (# See also: ...): the evidence code in merge_gate_support.py and the evidence-root export in merge_gate.sh point at each other and at FINDING-c2-5-pixels-red-under-gate. The stage must keep working on a bare run (no evidence override, no XDG_DATA_HOME) and never fail the gate because evidence could not be written: an unwritable root appends " (evidence not kept: <reason>)" to the detail, prints no EVIDENCE line, and the stage verdict is unchanged. STOP (ok=false, stop_reason): a file outside the list above; any test edit; a pin, threshold or tolerance you would have to change; a lint you would have to disable; a test that looks wrong ("test-defect: ..." form).\n' + BL + '\nDone when every test of ' + testFiles.join(', ') + ' is green with its controls, tests/specfactory fails exactly on the baseline set, python -m py_compile is clean on merge_gate_support.py and bash -n on merge_gate.sh, and the pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', testFiles.join(' ')) + ' ends PRE_GATE verdict OK; quote it. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the test lines, every constant, path and regex you added with its source), red_ids, parked.', { label: 'build:keepred', phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const build = await withRuling(mkBuild, tests.branch)
out = { ...out, build }
if (!(build && build.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build:keepred' }

phase('Check')
const check = SKIP['check:keepred'] ? { pass: true, evidence: 'skipped: check ok' } : await agent(RULES_PRE + '\nRole: gate checker (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only, detached worktree at origin/' + build.branch + ' (suffix chk-vg-keepred; remove it after with git worktree remove, no --force). Spec: ' + SPEC_D + '.' + IFACE_NOTE + '\n' + BL + '\n(1) The diff versus its merge base touches only ' + d.product.join(', ') + ' plus, from the merged test branch, ' + testFiles.join(', ') + '; list every other file (blocking). (2) Run ' + testFiles.join(', ') + ' and the whole tests/specfactory: PASS/FAIL per file with counts; the failing set equals the baseline. (3) POSITIVE CONTROLS: in a scratch copy revert the product files to the base: the new red cases go red again for the stated reason (' + d.red + '); list control by control. (4) THE DRY RUN (the gate\'s own stage on a fixture branch with a planted red): build a fixture tree under your own tmp dir with a planted red test file and a planted PNG-writing red test, then run the stage through its real CLI, e.g. ' + PY + ' scripts/specfactory/merge_gate_support.py playthrough <fixture tree> HEAD --python ' + PY + ' --timeout 120 --target <planted file> --force --no-setup (and lane_plays through its own CLI: --python, --timeout, --known-red, --lane-map only), with MERGE_GATE_EVIDENCE_ROOT set to a tmp dir (NEVER the real ~/Projects/om-push/gate-evidence), MERGE_GATE_START_UTC, MERGE_GATE_PIECE_ID (a comma list) and XDG_DATA_HOME on a tmp tree. The landing gate proves the evidence code only if a stage happens to reject, so THIS planted-red CLI run is the proof: do it for both stages (lane_plays through a git fixture repo and --lane-map, run with PATH set to a tmp bin dir holding only a git symlink and the venv python by absolute path, because xvfb-run and git are both in /usr/bin here; it has no --target/--force/--no-setup). Paste the stage\'s whole stdout (the REJECT line is the text merge_gate.sh prefixes with "GATE playthrough REJECT"; the EVIDENCE line follows it), the listing of the run directory it names (<stage>/pytest_rA.txt, the PNG, REPORT.txt with its env line) and the failing assertion line found inside the saved pytest output; then the same with a planted green: the stage prints OK, no EVIDENCE line, and the root has no new entry. Blocking if the EVIDENCE line is missing or names a path that is not where the ruling says, or if merge_gate.sh does not echo `GATE evidence kept: <path>` right after the REJECT line of both stages (show the lines). (5) PRE-GATE line format: run ' + PREGATE('<this worktree>', 'origin/main', testFiles.join(' ')) + ' and paste EVERY line; each is "PRE_GATE <step> OK|REJECT|WARN ..."; it must end PRE_GATE verdict OK; list each WARN. (6) QUESTIONS: ' + d.checkQs + ' ' + FG + ' (7) Every constant, path, regex and sentence added in the product diff, listed with its source (row, ledger, ruling item or file:line); blocking true for one with no source. (8) WIRED: state that the playthrough and lane_plays stages of merge_gate.sh reach the new code on a real gate run (name the lines), that the csim and transport commands carry MALLOC_PERTURB_=255 (name the lines), and what is NOT done (the look stage keeps no evidence: it never rejects; a timeout and a no-tests stage: what they leave). Report pass, blocking, evidence (every PASS/FAIL line, every pasted output).', { label: 'check:keepred', phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, check }
if (!(check && check.pass)) return { ...out, stopped: 'check:keepred' }

phase('Clerk')
const clerk = done('clerk:keepred') || await agent((LANDING ? 'LANDING RULE FOR THIS RUN (overrides section (b) where it differs): ' + LANDING + '\n' : '') + RULES + '\nRole: landing clerk (Engineer), rules.md section (b). The Dispatcher tells you at launch which landing rule applies (the temporary landing rule of dispatcher.md if it is on main). Piece ' + d.row + ' of ' + SPEC_D + '; tooling, no shot, no story_reviews row. ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'The push to main at the end IS authorised on a clean gate (Westley\'s standing word for clean-gate pushes, passed by the Dispatcher), subject to the known-red rule below. AT MOST ONE LANDING IN FLIGHT: the flock below serialises it.' : 'Do NOT push to main (args.pushMain false): branch only.') + ' DEPENDS CHECK, after git fetch origin and before the lock and before any gate: git show origin/main:' + PIECES_TOML + ', read depends_on of the ' + d.row + ' row and the state of HARNESS-gate-base-after-lock, the only blocking dependency (HARNESS-lane-plays-scope, HARNESS-coverage and HARNESS-westley-folder depend on this piece and are queued; whatever depends_on of the row still lists besides that id is reported, not blocking). If HARNESS-gate-base-after-lock is not attached on origin/main stop with ok=false, stop_reason "depends-not-attached: HARNESS-gate-base-after-lock": take no lock, run no gate, land nothing on main, but build, run the tests and the pre-gate and push the branch ' + LB + ' with everything done except the gate, the landing edits, the records commit and the push to main; write .wt-done; say so at the top of the summary. Branch ' + LB + ', suffix vg-keepred-land, from origin/main; merge origin/' + tests.branch + ', origin/' + build.branch + rulingMerge() + '. Stage files by name only; never a *.import or *.uid file; delete untracked .uid files before any checkout or merge. Conflicts: in ' + PIECES_TOML + ' take origin/main\'s side of every conflicting hunk (the row already carries this piece\'s owns); in ' + LEDGER + ' keep both sides; a row that appears more than once after the merge keeps one copy: drop byte-identical copies; if two copies of a row differ by any byte STOP and report the diff, never pick one. Any other conflict: STOP and report. Run ' + testFiles.join(', ') + ' and the whole tests/specfactory (' + PY + ' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/specfactory; PASS/FAIL per touched file): acceptance tests the gate cannot run for a comma list of pieces (the acceptance-ids and undertest steps WARN and skip: quote the WARN lines); the failing set must equal the baseline (' + (pre.baseline_red || []).join(', ') + '). Pre-gate before the lock (section (b)): ' + PREGATE('<landing worktree>', 'origin/main', testFiles.join(' ')) + '; it must end OK (a lint, footprint, owner-row or noise reject is fixed or reported before the lock, never spent on a full gate). Full gate EXACTLY section (b), detached into the background from the landing worktree, the lock taken first and origin/main fetched and merged inside it (main moves while a clerk waits for the lock): mkdir -p ~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-keepred; start the following in the background (run_in_background, so neither the lock wait nor the gate holds the foreground; the clerk waits on the lock without a timeout, flock with neither -w nor -n): flock ~/Projects/om-push/gate.lock env TMPDIR=$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-keepred MERGE_GATE_SUITE_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAYTHROUGH_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAY_TIMEOUT=900 MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<landing worktree>/' + PIECES_TOML + ' bash -c \'cd <landing worktree> && git fetch origin && git merge --no-edit origin/main && scripts/specfactory/pre_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + ' && scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + '\' >$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-keepred/gate.log 2>&1 (three positional arguments to each script; the last is ONE comma list with no spaces; add any further owner id a footprint line names and re-run the pre-gate; the pre-gate above is the cheap early check and pre_gate runs again inside the lock, on the tree after the merge; the script rejects a candidate that lacks the current origin/main, so a forgotten merge costs seconds, not a gate). The push to main is its own separate command run after the gate verdict: it is never chained (no && or ;) behind pre_gate.sh or merge_gate.sh. Wait for the completion notification of the background command without polling (no sleep loop, no pgrep, no repeated tail); when it arrives read gate.log. The gate ran only if gate.log holds a `GATE look` line and no `PRE_GATE REJECT` line (the in-lock chain is merge && pre_gate && merge_gate, so a failing merge or pre_gate leaves no GATE REJECT line and would read as clean); otherwise the gate did not run: stop with ok=false, stop_reason "gate-did-not-run", quote the tail of gate.log, push nothing to main. There is no VERDICT line: the verdict is the set of GATE <stage> REJECT lines; flake rule per section (b). This landing changes the gate\'s own playthrough and lane_plays stages and puts MALLOC_PERTURB_=255 on its csim and transport stages (baseline and branch runs alike): if a playthrough or lane_plays stage prints a REJECT, the new code printed `GATE evidence kept: <path>` right after it: quote both and look the directory up; if neither stage rejects, the landing gate proved nothing of the evidence code (the Check\'s planted-red CLI run is the proof): say so in the summary; a csim or transport reject is judged by the known-red rule below like any other. KNOWN-RED RULE (section (b), Architect 2026-10-12): push main only when EVERY GATE REJECT line (the csim regression stage prints "new failures: [...]") names ids that are lines of scripts/specfactory/gd_tests_known_red.txt or scripts/specfactory/lane_plays_known_red.txt on the landing tree (the lists are the rule; read them on the landing tree); a reject outside those files means branch only, ok=false, stop_reason "gate-reject", every REJECT line quoted, never a push. If no REJECT, or only listed ones: Right before the push: git fetch origin; if origin/main moved merge it in (say so; ledger appends keep both sides) and re-run the pre-gate, not the full gate. Push the branch ' + LB + ', then ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'as a separate command git push origin HEAD:main (only under the known-red rule)' : 'stop at the branch (args.pushMain false)') + '. RECORDS COMMIT after the merge (only when main was pushed): a second commit on the same branch (normal prose, attribution line), pushed to main the same way (fetch first, merge if moved, plain push, no force), holding ONLY: ' + PIECES_TOML + ' flip of ' + d.row + ' to status = { state = "attached", attach_sha = "<the landing sha7 pushed to main>" } (comment "landed <sha7>"); ' + LEDGER + ': on the day37 row FINDING-c2-5-pixels-red-under-gate APPEND one sentence "Evidence retention landed <date> at <sha7> (HARNESS-gate-keep-red-evidence): the next red playthrough or lane_plays stage leaves its pytest -rA output and PNGs under ~/Projects/om-push/gate-evidence/<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>-<piece>/ and a GATE evidence kept line names it; the csim and transport stages run under MALLOC_PERTURB_=255." and leave its status "under diagnosis" (it closes on the diagnosis, not here); do NOT touch FINDING-gate-base-before-lock (HARNESS-gate-base-after-lock closes it); LEDGER ROWS FOR THE DRAFTS: grep the ledger and the register for DRAFT-evidence-age and DRAFT-evidence-cap first; for each name with no hit add one row to the same ledger file (a new line in its table form, status "draft, Westley owns the number"): DRAFT-evidence-age = 7 days (merge_gate.sh --prune-evidence deletes older run directories; Architect 2026-10-21) and DRAFT-evidence-cap = 50 MiB (52,428,800 bytes) per stage subdirectory (oldest files dropped past it; Architect 2026-10-21), each naming merge_gate_support.py and merge_gate.sh as the sites; the programme file ' + PROGRAMME + ' only if its lane table has a row naming ' + d.row + ' (HARNESS-status owns it; else say so); write nothing about status anywhere else (no ROADMAP lane row, no journal line: the commit subject is the journal). Write NO script, args, launch or spec key into any pieces.toml row. Write .wt-done (date, branch, pushed sha) after the push; remove the worktree only if it is clean and its HEAD is contained in origin (git branch -r --contains HEAD), else leave it with .wt-done; delete only the merge_gate_before_* directories under your own TMPDIR. The report summary carries: the stage lines verbatim ("OK per stage" or every GATE REJECT line), the WARN lines, the test lines, main head, the records commit sha, and the plain statement of what is NOT done: the look stage keeps no evidence (it never rejects), and no automatic cleanup exists (the weekly auditor runs --prune-evidence). Report ok, branch, sha, summary, red_ids, stop_reason.' + IFACE_NOTE, { label: 'clerk:keepred', phase: 'Clerk', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, clerk }
if (clerk && /^depends-not-attached/.test(String(clerk.stop_reason || ''))) return { ...out, stopped: clerk.stop_reason, pushMain: false, next: LB + ' holds the piece (built, checked, pushed; nothing on main); when the depends_on ids named in the stop reason are attached, relaunch with args.skip for every finished step' }
if (!(clerk && clerk.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'clerk:keepred' }
return { ...out, pushMain: PUSH_MAIN, next: 'the next red playthrough or lane_plays stage keeps its evidence under ~/Projects/om-push/gate-evidence/ (diagnose FINDING-c2-5-pixels-red-under-gate from it); the drift auditor runs merge_gate.sh --prune-evidence weekly; HARNESS-lane-plays-scope, HARNESS-coverage and HARNESS-westley-folder (queued behind this piece) may then be built' }
